<title>USA: All American Food drops plan to sell shares.</title>
<headline>All American Food drops plan to sell shares.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, N.J. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>All American Food Group Inc said Thursday it had cancelled plans to sell an option to buy up to 1.0 million of its common shares.</p>
<p>It said it had rescinded the transaction, which it had intended to complete with foreign investor under an exemptive regulation of the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>It did not explain any reasons for its action.</p>
<p>All American Food is a franchiser of bagel stores under the name Goldberg's New York Bagels.</p>
